1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,180
Once upon a time, there was a sad love that would never be requited.

2
00:00:09,560 --> 00:00:13,840
But that alone does not give birth to a story.

3
00:00:14,540 --> 00:00:21,200
The man charged with the task of spinning this tale of love was no longer of this world.

4
00:00:21,960 --> 00:00:26,380
The story lives on with the love forever immersed in sorrow.

5
00:00:26,380 --> 00:00:34,000
Having lost its storyteller, the story is now wandering in search of its conclusion.

6
00:02:25,312 --> 00:02:50,632
Impressive. Truly a prodigy.

7
00:02:50,632 --> 00:02:53,872
Will a day come when I can dance like that too?

8
00:02:53,872 --> 00:02:56,872
Whoa, you finally got your head straight!

9
00:02:56,872 --> 00:02:58,872
What a wildly whimsical dream!

10
00:02:58,872 --> 00:03:00,872
That's the spirit, Dad!

11
00:03:00,872 --> 00:03:02,872
Molly is your strong suit!

12
00:03:02,872 --> 00:03:04,872
Pattern and dream big, right?

13
00:03:04,872 --> 00:03:06,872
Then you'll have bigger failures!

14
00:03:06,872 --> 00:03:08,872
Work hard and things work out!

15
00:03:08,872 --> 00:03:09,872
For normal people!

16
00:03:09,872 --> 00:03:13,872
Yeah, well, for now you gotta get out of that probationary class!

17
00:03:17,872 --> 00:03:22,872
That's right. When I'm Princess Tutu, I can dance any dance I want.

18
00:03:22,872 --> 00:03:26,872
What? But is that me? Or someone else?

19
00:03:26,872 --> 00:03:29,872
I'm just a girl in a probationary class.

20
00:03:29,872 --> 00:03:33,872
Or rather, when you get down to it, I'm just a duck.

21
00:03:33,872 --> 00:03:36,872
Maybe there's no point in me practicing.

22
00:03:36,872 --> 00:03:37,872
Oh?

23
00:03:37,872 --> 00:03:40,872
hundred bucks in my room!

24
00:03:40,872 --> 00:03:41,872
Let's go!

25
00:03:41,872 --> 00:03:42,872
You, baby!

26
00:03:42,872 --> 00:03:43,872
You're PengshDBQ!

27
00:03:43,872 --> 00:03:44,872
You, baby!

28
00:03:44,872 --> 00:03:58,872
I'm so obsessed with this.

29
00:03:58,872 --> 00:04:02,872
Watch out!

30
00:04:16,872 --> 00:04:19,872
Who are you? Are you calling to me?

31
00:04:21,872 --> 00:04:22,872
Fakir?

32
00:04:22,872 --> 00:04:24,872
What's with that look?

33
00:04:24,872 --> 00:04:26,872
Huh? What look?

34
00:04:26,872 --> 00:04:28,872
What were you thinking?

35
00:04:28,872 --> 00:04:29,872
What?

36
00:04:29,872 --> 00:04:31,872
Just now, what were you thinking?

37
00:04:32,872 --> 00:04:35,872
Someone. Someone's calling me.

38
00:04:35,872 --> 00:04:40,872
I don't know who it is, but I feel like I can understand what that person's feeling.

39
00:04:40,872 --> 00:04:42,872
The heartache deep down.

40
00:04:42,872 --> 00:04:45,872
A desire to see someone and talk to them.

41
00:04:45,872 --> 00:04:48,872
Feelings that I have too.

42
00:04:48,872 --> 00:04:52,872
Could this possibly be what it feels like to be lonely?

43
00:04:52,872 --> 00:04:54,872
What it feels like to be lonely?

44
00:04:54,872 --> 00:04:56,872
Muto's regaining his heart.

45
00:04:57,872 --> 00:04:58,872
Look at this face!

46
00:04:58,872 --> 00:05:01,872
I hate this face and its feelings.

47
00:05:01,872 --> 00:05:04,872
This wretched face wallowing in its loneliness.

48
00:05:04,872 --> 00:05:06,872
Is it fun recalling such emotions?

49
00:05:06,872 --> 00:05:08,872
Does it feel good, Muto?

50
00:05:08,872 --> 00:05:09,872
No.

51
00:05:10,872 --> 00:05:14,872
Right. You have no need of a heart, Muto. None whatsoever.

52
00:05:14,872 --> 00:05:17,872
If you were to regain such a thing.

53
00:05:17,872 --> 00:05:18,872
If I were.

54
00:05:18,872 --> 00:05:20,872
Don't fall for such a fool's hope.

55
00:05:20,872 --> 00:05:21,872
Got that?

56
00:05:21,872 --> 00:05:22,872
Yes.

57
00:05:22,872 --> 00:05:23,872
Speak louder.

58
00:05:23,872 --> 00:05:24,872
Understood.

59
00:05:24,872 --> 00:05:26,872
I will do as you say, Fakir.

60
00:05:26,872 --> 00:05:28,872
Good. As it should be.

61
00:05:28,872 --> 00:05:37,872
Miss Duck, as punishment for disturbing the advanced class, you will practice the develope. Am I understood?

62
00:05:37,872 --> 00:05:38,872
Yes, sir.

63
00:05:38,872 --> 00:05:41,872
If you practice earnestly, I'll put you back with the beginners.

64
00:05:41,872 --> 00:05:42,872
Oh, yes, sir.

65
00:05:42,872 --> 00:05:43,872
Practice poorly, though.

66
00:05:43,872 --> 00:05:46,872
And I'll have you marry me forthwith!

67
00:05:50,872 --> 00:05:53,872
I'm a bird on probation, plus I have to stay late.

68
00:05:53,872 --> 00:05:56,872
At this rate, I may never get to be like Rue.

69
00:05:56,872 --> 00:05:58,872
Oh, it's Muto.

70
00:06:03,872 --> 00:06:05,872
Princess Tutu.

71
00:06:05,872 --> 00:06:07,872
That's just a story.

72
00:06:07,872 --> 00:06:10,872
She's still a princess fated, never to be with her prince.

73
00:06:10,872 --> 00:06:14,872
When she confesses her love, she turns into a speck of light and vanishes.

74
00:06:14,872 --> 00:06:17,872
That's just what happens to Tutu in the story.

75
00:06:17,872 --> 00:06:19,872
The story isn't reality.

76
00:06:19,872 --> 00:06:23,872
Though it is true that Muto is a prince from inside a story.

77
00:06:23,872 --> 00:06:25,872
Oh, who cares?

78
00:06:25,872 --> 00:06:27,872
It doesn't matter if the story is real or not.

79
00:06:27,872 --> 00:06:31,872
All I want to do is find the pieces of Muto's heart and give them back to him.

80
00:06:31,872 --> 00:06:32,872
That's right.

81
00:06:32,872 --> 00:06:36,872
I'm not thinking about being with him or confessing to him or anything.

82
00:06:36,872 --> 00:06:38,872
I'm not thinking about any of that!

83
00:06:38,872 --> 00:06:56,872
I don't really understand.

84
00:06:56,872 --> 00:07:01,872
It's okay. You can be a dummy, Muto. Now and forever.

85
00:07:01,872 --> 00:07:04,872
Trust me, Muto. You do love me.

86
00:07:04,872 --> 00:07:08,872
Oh, okay. Then I do love you.

87
00:07:08,872 --> 00:07:10,872
Yes. Yes, remember that.

88
00:07:10,872 --> 00:07:15,872
You don't need to understand. And you don't need a heart either.

89
00:07:15,872 --> 00:07:16,872
What?

90
00:07:16,872 --> 00:07:19,872
This feeling of wanting to see someone and talk to them.

91
00:07:19,872 --> 00:07:22,872
It stays even when I'm with you.

92
00:07:22,872 --> 00:07:25,872
Could this possibly be the feeling of loneliness?

93
00:07:25,872 --> 00:07:30,872
I don't know. These emotions I'm feeling.

94
00:07:30,872 --> 00:07:31,872
Room!

95
00:07:31,872 --> 00:07:34,872
Would you please stop making him recall stupid things?

96
00:07:34,872 --> 00:07:37,872
Muto, go back to your room.

97
00:07:37,872 --> 00:07:38,872
Okay.

98
00:07:39,872 --> 00:07:43,872
You'd better not be the person who's helping him dredge up these weird things.

99
00:07:43,872 --> 00:07:44,872
Oh, please.

100
00:07:44,872 --> 00:07:46,872
Who else are you saying could have done it?

101
00:07:46,872 --> 00:07:52,872
Maybe it was Princess Tutu from the fairy tale. Maybe she appeared in real life.

102
00:07:52,872 --> 00:07:56,872
Quiet. Try to stay away from Muto from now on.

103
00:07:56,872 --> 00:07:59,872
Stop trying to order me around.

104
00:07:59,872 --> 00:08:04,872
Huh? Piano? Where's Tuck?

105
00:08:04,872 --> 00:08:14,872
Is that Tuck?

106
00:08:14,872 --> 00:08:16,872
Oh, why are you two here?

107
00:08:16,872 --> 00:08:18,872
Hey, hey, that's our line.

108
00:08:18,872 --> 00:08:23,872
That's right. We came here thinking you would be really depressed because you had to stay behind.

109
00:08:23,872 --> 00:08:25,872
Why are you so chipper?

110
00:08:25,872 --> 00:08:29,872
Thank you both. But I'm really having a lot of fun right now.

111
00:08:29,872 --> 00:08:33,872
Because the more you practice dancing, the more fun it becomes.

112
00:08:33,872 --> 00:08:34,872
You don't!

113
00:08:34,872 --> 00:08:36,872
Don't force it!

114
00:08:36,872 --> 00:08:41,872
You can act sad when you're sad or like you're in pain when you're suffering.

115
00:08:41,872 --> 00:08:43,872
Oh, you were suffering then.

116
00:08:43,872 --> 00:08:45,872
Well, it was your fault.

117
00:08:45,872 --> 00:08:46,872
No.

118
00:08:46,872 --> 00:08:47,872
Are you okay?

119
00:08:47,872 --> 00:08:49,872
Yeah, I'm okay.

120
00:08:49,872 --> 00:08:52,872
Say, why don't we keep her company?

121
00:08:52,872 --> 00:08:53,872
Huh?

122
00:08:53,872 --> 00:08:54,872
Yeah, good idea.

123
00:08:54,872 --> 00:08:55,872
What?

124
00:08:55,872 --> 00:08:56,872
Th-thank you.

125
00:08:56,872 --> 00:08:59,872
It's fine. After all, this is for you.

126
00:08:59,872 --> 00:09:02,872
Okay, let's all drop the probationary class with Duck.

127
00:09:06,872 --> 00:09:09,872
You still have a long way to go, Duck.

128
00:09:09,872 --> 00:09:10,872
Oh.

129
00:09:12,872 --> 00:09:13,872
Miss Duck!

130
00:09:13,872 --> 00:09:15,872
M-Mr. Cat!

131
00:09:15,872 --> 00:09:17,872
I have some unfortunate news.

132
00:09:17,872 --> 00:09:18,872
M-Unfortunate news?

133
00:09:18,872 --> 00:09:19,872
Yes, Miss Duck.

134
00:09:19,872 --> 00:09:34,872
You have worked much too hard. Therefore, unfortunately, I must put off having you marry me!

135
00:09:34,872 --> 00:09:36,872
Uh, oh, I see then.

136
00:09:36,872 --> 00:09:37,872
And?

137
00:09:37,872 --> 00:09:41,872
I will let you return to the beginner class.

138
00:09:41,872 --> 00:09:42,872
What?

139
00:09:42,872 --> 00:09:43,872
Uh?

140
00:09:43,872 --> 00:09:45,872
Uh, thank you so much!

141
00:09:45,872 --> 00:09:46,872
You did it!

142
00:09:46,872 --> 00:09:47,872
I'm so happy for you!

143
00:09:47,872 --> 00:09:48,872
Good job!

144
00:09:48,872 --> 00:09:49,872
All right!

145
00:09:49,872 --> 00:09:50,872
Go!

146
00:09:56,872 --> 00:09:58,872
The wind's picking up.

147
00:09:58,872 --> 00:09:59,872
Hm?

148
00:09:59,872 --> 00:10:00,872
Oh, Muto!

149
00:10:00,872 --> 00:10:07,872
What is it you want me to do?

150
00:10:07,872 --> 00:10:09,872
Who are you talking to?

151
00:10:17,872 --> 00:10:19,872
W-what was...

152
00:10:19,872 --> 00:10:20,872
Uh...

153
00:10:20,872 --> 00:10:21,872
Muto?

154
00:10:21,872 --> 00:10:22,872
Huh?

155
00:10:22,872 --> 00:10:23,872
Where...

156
00:10:23,872 --> 00:10:24,872
Muto!

157
00:10:24,872 --> 00:10:26,872
Uh, he's gone.

158
00:10:26,872 --> 00:10:27,872
Muto!

159
00:10:27,872 --> 00:10:30,872
What are you doing?

160
00:10:30,872 --> 00:10:32,872
I'm sorry.

161
00:10:32,872 --> 00:10:33,872
Huh?

162
00:10:33,872 --> 00:10:34,872
Huh?

163
00:10:34,872 --> 00:10:35,872
He's...

164
00:10:35,872 --> 00:10:36,872
Not there!

165
00:10:36,872 --> 00:10:38,872
Were you just calling for Muto?

166
00:10:38,872 --> 00:10:39,872
Uh...

167
00:10:39,872 --> 00:10:40,872
Yeah.

168
00:10:40,872 --> 00:10:41,872
You need something?

169
00:10:41,872 --> 00:10:42,872
No, not need.

170
00:10:42,872 --> 00:10:43,872
But...

171
00:10:43,872 --> 00:10:45,872
I just saw him come out this way.

172
00:10:45,872 --> 00:10:46,872
What?

173
00:10:46,872 --> 00:10:47,872
There was no one coming out.

174
00:10:47,872 --> 00:10:50,872
B-but I'm sure I saw Muto!

175
00:10:50,872 --> 00:10:51,872
No way.

176
00:10:51,872 --> 00:10:53,872
I didn't see anyone out here.

177
00:10:53,872 --> 00:10:54,872
So...

178
00:10:54,872 --> 00:10:55,872
That way then?

179
00:10:55,872 --> 00:10:56,872
It was you.

180
00:10:56,872 --> 00:10:57,872
Huh?

181
00:10:57,872 --> 00:11:00,872
You cried out rudely when I was dancing and interrupted me.

182
00:11:00,872 --> 00:11:01,872
Oh!

183
00:11:01,872 --> 00:11:02,872
Well that was...

184
00:11:02,872 --> 00:11:06,872
You don't seem to have the slightest comprehension as to how much focus is required when dancing.

185
00:11:06,872 --> 00:11:07,872
Oh!

186
00:11:07,872 --> 00:11:09,872
If it's about that, sorry!

187
00:11:09,872 --> 00:11:12,872
But more importantly, Muto is acting weird just now.

188
00:11:12,872 --> 00:11:13,872
Or rather acting strange.

189
00:11:13,872 --> 00:11:14,872
That's the same.

190
00:11:14,872 --> 00:11:17,872
But anyway, I gotta find him now!

191
00:11:17,872 --> 00:11:18,872
See ya!

192
00:11:18,872 --> 00:11:19,872
Hold on!

193
00:11:19,872 --> 00:11:20,872
We aren't done talking yet!

194
00:11:20,872 --> 00:11:22,872
Wait just a minute!

195
00:11:22,872 --> 00:11:23,872
Muto!

196
00:11:23,872 --> 00:11:36,872
You need to stay away from Ruu.

197
00:11:36,872 --> 00:11:37,872
Muto?

198
00:11:37,872 --> 00:11:38,872
It's strange.

199
00:11:38,872 --> 00:11:39,872
Definitely strange.

200
00:11:39,872 --> 00:11:52,872
After talking to someone invisible, it's like time skipped forward and Muto...

201
00:11:52,872 --> 00:11:54,872
I wonder which way he went.

202
00:11:54,872 --> 00:11:55,872
Uh...

203
00:11:55,872 --> 00:11:56,872
Ruu?

204
00:11:56,872 --> 00:11:57,872
Your...

205
00:11:57,872 --> 00:11:58,872
Your name...

206
00:11:58,872 --> 00:11:59,872
It's stuck, right?

207
00:11:59,872 --> 00:12:00,872
You run pretty...

208
00:12:00,872 --> 00:12:01,872
Pretty fast!

209
00:12:01,872 --> 00:12:02,872
Yeah!

210
00:12:02,872 --> 00:12:03,872
I know!

211
00:12:03,872 --> 00:12:04,872
Don't mock me!

212
00:12:04,872 --> 00:12:06,872
I'm just a little out of breath, okay?

213
00:12:06,872 --> 00:12:07,872
So just...

214
00:12:07,872 --> 00:12:08,872
Cut it out!

215
00:12:08,872 --> 00:12:09,872
Okay!

216
00:12:09,872 --> 00:12:10,872
Sorry!

217
00:12:10,872 --> 00:12:11,872
Oh!

218
00:12:11,872 --> 00:12:12,872
What is it?

219
00:12:12,872 --> 00:12:29,872
Since there are two of us here, I was thinking maybe it'd be faster if we split up and search

220
00:12:29,872 --> 00:12:30,872
separately.

221
00:12:30,872 --> 00:12:31,872
That's true!

222
00:12:31,872 --> 00:12:32,872
You're quite right.

223
00:12:32,872 --> 00:12:37,872
It's rather odd that someone like you and I should be walking shoulder to shoulder to

224
00:12:37,872 --> 00:12:38,872
begin with.

225
00:12:38,872 --> 00:12:39,872
Odd?

226
00:12:39,872 --> 00:12:40,872
Yeah, she's right.

227
00:12:40,872 --> 00:12:41,872
Oh!

228
00:12:41,872 --> 00:12:43,872
Well, I'll go look over here.

229
00:12:43,872 --> 00:12:46,872
We can decide on a time or something and meet up somewhere.

230
00:12:46,872 --> 00:12:47,872
I changed my mind!

231
00:12:47,872 --> 00:12:48,872
What?

232
00:12:48,872 --> 00:12:49,872
Why is that?

233
00:12:49,872 --> 00:12:53,872
It's much more reliable with two pairs of eyes looking.

234
00:12:53,872 --> 00:12:54,872
Hmm...

235
00:12:54,872 --> 00:12:55,872
Ya think?

236
00:12:55,872 --> 00:12:56,872
Um...

237
00:12:56,872 --> 00:12:57,872
What is it now?

238
00:12:57,872 --> 00:13:02,872
Have you been friends with Mewto for a long time now?

239
00:13:02,872 --> 00:13:03,872
You keep calling him Mewto.

240
00:13:03,872 --> 00:13:04,872
That's awfully forward of you.

241
00:13:04,872 --> 00:13:05,872
But Mewto told me that I could.

242
00:13:05,872 --> 00:13:06,872
And another thing.

243
00:13:06,872 --> 00:13:08,872
We're not exactly friends, so I'd appreciate it if you didn't call me Roo.

244
00:13:08,872 --> 00:13:09,872
Then what am I supposed to call you?

245
00:13:09,872 --> 00:13:10,872
Lady Roo.

246
00:13:10,872 --> 00:13:11,872
Hmm...

247
00:13:11,872 --> 00:13:12,872
Lady Roo.

248
00:13:12,872 --> 00:13:13,872
Hmm...

249
00:13:13,872 --> 00:13:14,872
Lady...

250
00:13:14,872 --> 00:13:15,872
Roo?

251
00:13:15,872 --> 00:13:16,872
What?

252
00:13:16,872 --> 00:13:17,872
What's so hard about that?

253
00:13:17,872 --> 00:13:18,872
It's just weird.

254
00:13:18,872 --> 00:13:19,872
I'll call you Roo.

255
00:13:19,872 --> 00:13:20,872
It's cuter that way.

256
00:13:20,872 --> 00:13:21,872
Cuter?

257
00:13:21,872 --> 00:13:24,872
Besides, we've walked together and talked all this time, so we're already friends now.

258
00:13:24,872 --> 00:13:25,872
Thus it's Roo.

259
00:13:25,872 --> 00:13:26,872
Still no Mewto.

260
00:13:26,872 --> 00:13:27,872
Huh?

261
00:13:27,872 --> 00:13:28,872
What?

262
00:13:28,872 --> 00:13:29,872
I'll call you Roo.

263
00:13:29,872 --> 00:13:30,872
It's cuter that way.

264
00:13:30,872 --> 00:13:31,872
Cuter?

265
00:13:31,872 --> 00:13:35,872
Besides, we've walked together and talked all this time, so we're already friends now.

266
00:13:35,872 --> 00:13:36,872
Thus it's Roo.

267
00:13:36,872 --> 00:13:37,872
Still no Mewto.

268
00:13:37,872 --> 00:13:38,872
Huh, Roo?

269
00:13:38,872 --> 00:13:39,872
Hmph.

270
00:13:39,872 --> 00:13:40,872
What's that?

271
00:13:40,872 --> 00:13:41,872
They're all...

272
00:13:41,872 --> 00:13:42,872
all crying.

273
00:13:42,872 --> 00:13:45,872
It's a funeral, so naturally.

274
00:13:45,872 --> 00:13:46,872
Mewto!

275
00:13:46,872 --> 00:13:47,872
Mewto!

276
00:13:47,872 --> 00:13:48,872
Mewto!

277
00:13:48,872 --> 00:13:49,872
Mewto!

278
00:13:49,872 --> 00:13:50,872
Mewto!

279
00:13:50,872 --> 00:13:51,872
Mewto!

280
00:13:51,872 --> 00:13:52,872
Mewto!

281
00:13:52,872 --> 00:13:53,872
Mewto!

